{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "gray 4-connected candidate object s below the blue structure",
  "dst": "lower black pocket component d inside the blue structure bbox",
  "match_cond": "some rotation of s covers all cells of d while any extra cells stay on black cells and do not overlap blue",
  "transform": "recolor matched gray objects red; leave unmatched gray objects unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 12x12, background black, colors {blue, gray} in input; output replaces matched gray with red
  blue_band:
    shape: 3 rows spanning full grid width (cols 0-11)
    top_row_position: row 1-4 [observed]
    structure: 1-2 Pi-shaped arches; top row = arch ceilings (contiguous blue, width 3-4); mid row = arch walls (only endpoint cols blue); bottom row = base (mostly blue, cols 0 and 11 always blue, gaps only at pocket openings)
    black_components: pockets (touch bottom row, span mid+bottom rows only, size 2-4) and non-pockets (touch top row only, above arches)
    pockets_per_band: 1-2, each pocket sits below one arch; pocket cols = arch interior cols in mid row, possibly wider in bottom row
  gray_objects:
    count: 2-4
    size: 3-8 cells each, 4-connected
    position: below blue band, rows 7-10 [observed]; gap of 1-4 empty rows between band bottom and first gray row
    separation: mutually non-adjacent (no shared 4-neighbor), non-adjacent to blue
    last_row: row 11 always empty [observed]
  rule:
    for each gray object, try all 4 rotations x all translations; if any placement covers every cell of some pocket without overlapping blue or leaving the grid, recolor that gray object red
    at least 1 matched (red) and 1 unmatched (stays gray) per example

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first; build pockets first, then construct matching/non-matching gray objects
  steps:
    1. Pick 1-2 arches with width 3-4 each. Place them in a 3-row band at rows r0 to r0+2 (r0 in 1-4). Build top row (arch ceilings), mid row (walls only), bottom row (full-width blue base with gaps at/near arch interiors). Verify pockets are 4-connected black components touching bottom row, size 2-4.
    2. For each pocket, create 1+ gray objects that can cover it under some rotation (object >= pocket, superset placement exists avoiding blue). Also create 1+ gray objects that cannot cover any pocket (wrong shape/size/orientation with no valid non-blue placement).
    3. Place gray objects in rows 7-10, separated by >=1 black col gap, non-adjacent to each other and to blue. Ensure >=1 matched and >=1 unmatched.
    4. Derive output by running the rotation+placement check and recoloring matched gray to red.
